<title>DUBAI: Saudi Aramco revises bunker fuel prices.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco revises bunker fuel prices.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has cut A-960 bunker fuel from Ras Tanura and Dammam by $1 a tonne to $101 ($15.50 a barrel) effective July 17, the firm said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A-888 from the two ports is cut by $3 to $196 a tonne.</p>
<p>Sales of A-960 from Jeddah and Yanbu are increased $2 a tonne to $96 ($14.74). A-888 is unchanged at $180 a tonne.</p>
</text>
